      "accepted": [
        "personSession",
        "everIdToken",
        "everIdTokenProductUi"
      ],
      "why": "A person's app.ever.co session, an Ever ID token of the Ever Platform project from a sign-in at most 300 s old, or (the in-product consent path) a step-up Ever ID token from the installation's own client (inst-<instance id>, or an Ever Cloud product client configured for an installation Ever operates), signed in at most 300 s ago, of an owner or admin, for that installation only and never for counterparty_discoverable or instance_url; such a consent records consent_source product_ui. Any other token a product, an installation or an App obtained is refused with 403 session_required, and a product may still send its admin to app.ever.co with the signed link of instanceGetConsentUrl. No installation calls this operation with its instance token. The operation's limits (Idempotency-Key, the person rate class, a 16 KiB body, the closed body, current scope and agreement versions) are stated in the pinned contract."
